==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|s|ä}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*sää}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*śäŋe}} ( ~ {{m|urj-pro|*śäkV}}, {{m|urj-pro|*śäɣV}}, {{m|urj-pro|*śäwV}} - if Finn. does not belong). Baltic-Finnic cognates of the same meaning are deemed certain and include eg. {{cog|krl|seä}}, {{cog|krl|siä}}, {{cog|krl|šiä}}, {{cog|vot|sää}}, {{cog|vep|sä}}. Probably inherited from {{der|fi|fiu-pro|*säŋi||air}}, also reflected in {{cog|hu|ég||sky}} and {{cog|kpv|сынӧд||warm air}}.

====Noun====
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[weather]]
#:* [[hyvä]]llä ''säällä'' = in good ''weather''
#:* [[huono]]lla ''säällä'' = in bad ''weather''

